# AC surface (AC.BAG.1 – AC.BAG.7 + AC.BAG.S + AC.AG.1 –
# AC.AG.5 + AC.A4.settings_merge) — outcome-shaped per the locked
# plan-doc §4. Behaviour count = 14; ACs declared = 14. Forward +
# reverse match. Universal classes (B2, B5) fire regardless of
# mode; DEV-MODE-only classes (B1, B3, B4, T1, T2, T3) fire only
# in dev-mode workspaces.
#
# Mode-aware partition (programme D4 lock + plan §6 D-A4.5):
# secret-commit + blast-radius gates are user-protective in every
# workspace (UNIVERSAL); ODD-discipline gates (--amend in agent
# context, pos-amend dry-run gating, wrong-tree-write, wrong-WD
# dispatch, method-enumerated prompt, dispatch-staleness) are
# pos-v2-dev-specific (DEV-MODE-only). Each gate script's first
# action is the universal-leg check (returning before the mode-
# bit read for the universal classes); the DEV-MODE-leg fires
# only after the mode-bit confirms `dev-mode`.
#
# Override mechanism (D-A4.6): env var `POS_BASH_GUARD_ALLOW=1`
# admits B1, B3, B4 ONLY (DEV-MODE-only Bash classes). UNIVERSAL
# classes (B2 secret, B5 blast-radius) are NOT bypassable —
# constraint 18 enforces the property; AC.BAG.1 + AC.BAG.2 name
# the no-override behaviour explicitly.
#
# Length threshold for T2 (AC.AG.2): 2500 characters, NAMED in
# the AC text per the plan §4 + D-A4.7 ruling. Threshold is
# auditable (not method per ODD §7.4).
#
# T3 detection method (D-A4.8): union of (a) amendment-number
# regex + manifest-table query AND (b) AC-ID regex + manifest-
# table query AND (c) git-log fallback when manifest doesn't
# return the named row. Fail-closed-to-permissive at the manifest-
# import boundary (tracker unreachable → fall through to allow,
# mirrors A2's R7).
#
# Hook-chain ordering: A2 first, A3 second on Edit|Write|MultiEdit;
# A4_bash on Bash; A4_task on Task. Claude Code admits multiple
# matcher entries; each fires only on its matching tool surface.
# No cross-matcher interference. A2's + A3's existing AC.OBG.x +
# AC.TDG.x tests are untouched (regression contract).
#
# Audit log shape (D-A4.9 method per ODD §7.4): NDJSON at
# `<workspace>/workspace/.pos/bash-guard.log` +
# `<workspace>/workspace/.pos/agent-guard.log` mirroring A2's
# objective-binding-gate.log + A3's tdd-guard.log pattern. Atomic
# append via POSIX O_APPEND for writes < PIPE_BUF.
#
# Self-bootstrap order followed (locked plan hard constraint 15):
# (a) tracker manifest rows registered for AC.BAG.1..AC.BAG.S +
# AC.AG.1..AC.AG.5 + AC.A4.settings_merge BEFORE first source
